<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Middlesex</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Middlesex is a historic county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, north and west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">City of London</a>, between the Thames and the Lea. Its name means 'the Middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a>', and in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it formed part of the kingdom of Essex before passing under Mercian control. Most of it was absorbed into Greater London in 1965.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/middlesex.jpg" alt="Middlesex" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The College of Arms · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Middlesex.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
